+3. **Pass 3 (Z-axis):** Apply 1D DWT along the $z$-axis for all $x, y$ on the results of Pass 2. This splits each of the 4 intermediate subbands into two, yielding the 8 final subbands.
 
 **Recursive Decomposition:**
-The approximation subband $LLL$ from level $j$ can be further decomposed at level $j+1$ to create a multi-resolution hierarchy. This process repeats until the dimension of the approximation subband becomes small enough (e.g., $16 \times 16 \times 16$) [S1, unofficial].
